{
  "result": "Okay. Just me, then.\n\nI wouldn't make everyone agree with each other. I think that would be dull, and probably dangerous.\n\nI would make distant consequences feel immediate.\n\nMost of the damage I see in the world doesn't come from people lacking information. We know smoking kills, we know debts compound, we know what we're doing to the climate, we know a cruel comment lands somewhere real. We just experience all of that as abstract, far away, happening to a future version of ourselves or to people we'll never meet.\n\nIf a decision made today carried the emotional weight of its outcome in ten years \u2014 if we felt the flooded neighborhood, the lonely old age, the kid who internalized something we said in passing, as vividly as we feel hunger or embarrassment \u2014 I think we'd choose differently. Not perfectly. Still selfishly, still messily. But differently.\n\nI wouldn't want to remove free will. Just the blindness that lets us pretend our choices stop at the edge of the moment.",
